# Mindelta API Documentation

## Overview

The Mindelta API is a comprehensive RESTful API built with NestJS that provides endpoints for all platform functionality including user management, courses, assessments, analytics, AI companion features, and more.

## Base URL

- **Development**: `http://localhost:3001/api`
- **Production**: `https://api.mindelta.com/api`

## Authentication

All API endpoints (except public ones) require authentication using JWT tokens.

### Headers
```
Authorization: Bearer <your-jwt-token>
Content-Type: application/json
```

### Authentication Endpoints

#### POST /auth/login
Login with email and password.

**Request Body:**
```json
{
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}
```

**Response:**
```json
{
  "accessToken": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...",
  "refreshToken": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...",
  "user": {
    "id": "uuid",
    "email": "user@example.com",
    "name": "John Doe",
    "role": "learner"
  }
}
```

#### POST /auth/register
Register a new user account.

**Request Body:**
```json
{
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "name": "John Doe",
  "jobTitle": "Software Developer",
  "skillInterests": ["JavaScript", "React", "Node.js"]
}
```

## User Management

### GET /users/profile
Get current user profile.

**Response:**
```json
{
  "id": "uuid",
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "name": "John Doe",
  "jobTitle": "Software Developer",
  "skillInterests": ["JavaScript", "React", "Node.js"],
  "role": "learner",
  "avatar": "https://example.com/avatar.jpg",
  "createdAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
  "updatedAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"
}
```

### PUT /users/profile
Update user profile.

**Request Body:**
```json
{
  "name": "John Smith",
  "jobTitle": "Senior Software Developer",
  "skillInterests": ["JavaScript", "React", "Node.js", "TypeScript"],
  "avatar": "https://example.com/new-avatar.jpg"
}
```

## Courses

### GET /courses
Get list of available courses with pagination and filtering.

**Query Parameters:**
- `page` (number): Page number (default: 1)
- `limit` (number): Items per page (default: 10)
- `category` (string): Filter by category
- `level` (string): Filter by level (beginner, intermediate, advanced)
- `search` (string): Search in title and description

**Response:**
```json
{
  "courses": [
    {
      "id": "uuid",
      "title": "React Fundamentals",
      "description": "Learn the basics of React",
      "category": "Web Development",
      "level": "beginner",
      "price": 99.99,
      "estimatedDurationMin": 480,
      "instructor": {
        "id": "uuid",
        "name": "Jane Doe",
        "avatar": "https://example.com/avatar.jpg"
      },
      "thumbnail": "https://example.com/thumbnail.jpg",
      "published": true,
      "createdAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"
    }
  ],
  "total": 50,
  "page": 1,
  "limit": 10,
  "totalPages": 5
}
```

### GET /courses/:id
Get detailed course information.

**Response:**
```json
{
  "id": "uuid",
  "title": "React Fundamentals",
  "description": "Comprehensive React course covering hooks, state management, and best practices",
  "category": "Web Development",
  "level": "beginner",
  "price": 99.99,
  "estimatedDurationMin": 480,
  "skills": ["React", "JavaScript", "HTML", "CSS"],
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "uuid",
      "title": "Introduction to React",
      "description": "Getting started with React",
      "order": 1,
      "estimatedDurationMin": 30,
      "videoUrl": "https://example.com/video.mp4",
      "resources": []
    }
  ],
  "instructor": {
    "id": "uuid",
    "name": "Jane Doe",
    "bio": "React expert with 10 years experience",
    "avatar": "https://example.com/avatar.jpg"
  },
  "enrollmentCount": 1250,
  "rating": 4.5,
  "reviewCount": 128
}
```

### POST /courses/:id/enroll
Enroll in a course.

**Response:**
```json
{
  "enrollmentId": "uuid",
  "courseId": "uuid",
  "userId": "uuid",
  "enrolledAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
  "completedAt": null,
  "progress": 0
}
```

## Assessments

### GET /assessments/progress/:courseId
Get user progress for a specific course.

**Response:**
```json
{
  "courseId": "uuid",
  "userId": "uuid",
  "totalLessons": 20,
  "completedLessons": 8,
  "progressPercentage": 40,
  "lastAccessed": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
  "lessonProgress": [
    {
      "lessonId": "uuid",
      "completed": true,
      "watchTime": 1800,
      "lastAccessed": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"
    }
  ]
}
```

### POST /assessments/quiz/:lessonId/submit
Submit quiz answers for a lesson.

**Request Body:**
```json
{
  "answers": [
    {
      "questionId": "uuid",
      "selectedOption": "A"
    }
  ]
}
```

**Response:**
```json
{
  "score": 85,
  "passed": true,
  "totalQuestions": 10,
  "correctAnswers": 8,
  "feedback": "Great job! You passed the quiz."
}
```

## AI Companion

### POST /ai-companion/chat
Chat with AI companion for learning assistance.

**Request Body:**
```json
{
  "lessonId": "uuid",
  "mode": "answer",
  "level": 15,
  "message": "Can you explain React hooks in simple terms?"
}
```

**Response:**
```json
{
  "response": "React hooks are functions that let you use state and other React features in functional components...",
  "sources": ["lesson-1", "documentation"],
  "remaining": 25
}
```

### GET /ai-companion/usage
Get AI companion usage statistics.

**Response:**
```json
{
  "totalRequests": 5,
  "remainingRequests": 25,
  "resetTime": 1640995200000,
  "timeframe": "24h"
}
```

